WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:16.952
go!" Henry said to Maggie.

2
00:00:17.912 --> 00:00:20.294
Without waiting for her, he rushed over to Kyle.

3
00:00:21.175 --> 00:00:23.157
Coach Phillips was hurrying toward him too.

4
00:00:24.158 --> 00:00:27.821
Everyone else had stopped whatever they were doing and turned to stare.

5
00:00:27.841 --> 00:00:29.722
"What happened?"

6
00:00:30.082 --> 00:00:31.804
Henry asked when he reached Kyle.

7
00:00:32.728 --> 00:00:36.049
Kyle's large blue gym bag was sitting on a chair near the pool.

8
00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:38.891
Its zipper was halfway open.

9
00:00:39.891 --> 00:00:43.813
When Henry looked down into the opening, he saw a puddle of green.

10
00:00:44.813 --> 00:00:49.835
The green paint was all over Kyle's sneakers, T-shirt, and other belongings.

11
00:00:49.855 --> 00:00:53.296
"All my stuff is ruined!"

12
00:00:53.657 --> 00:00:54.657
Kyle complained.

13
00:00:55.637 --> 00:00:56.778
The coach reached them.

14
00:00:56.798 --> 00:00:58.819
"This is outrageous!"

15
00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.760
he exclaimed as he looked into Kyle's bag.

16
00:01:02.848 --> 00:01:03.989
Then he spun around.

17
00:01:04.009 --> 00:01:07.591
"Someone had better confess right now!

18
00:01:08.572 --> 00:01:10.433
Otherwise I'm going to cancel these tryouts!"

19
00:01:11.694 --> 00:01:12.575
"Oh no!"

20
00:01:13.015 --> 00:01:14.056
Daisy exclaimed.

21
00:01:15.056 --> 00:01:18.499
Kyle glared at Cole, who was standing a short distance away.

22
00:01:18.519 --> 00:01:20.180
"It was him!"

23
00:01:20.540 --> 00:01:21.761
he said, pointing.

24
00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:26.004
"Everyone knows he's the one who dumped those frogs in the pool.

25
00:01:27.044 --> 00:01:28.265
He must have done this too!

26
00:01:29.706 --> 00:01:32.028
He's afraid I'll beat him for that spot on the team!"

27
00:01:33.088 --> 00:01:34.789
"Cole didn't do anything!"

28
00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:35.770
Maggie said.

29
00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:39.312
"You probably put that paint there yourself, Kyle!

30
00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.234
If there's any paint in your bag, that is."

31
00:01:43.475 --> 00:01:47.898
Henry realized that nobody could see the paint except for him, Kyle, and the coach.

32
00:01:49.079 --> 00:01:51.741
"There's really paint in here, Maggie," he said.

33
00:01:51.761 --> 00:01:55.123
"The only question is how it got there."

34
00:01:55.143 --> 00:01:58.345
"Yes," Coach Phillips agreed.

35
00:01:58.365 --> 00:02:02.388
"And I want an answer to that question right now!

36
00:02:03.548 --> 00:02:06.489
I also want to know who brought those frogs to the pool."

37
00:02:07.490 --> 00:02:09.691
Just then Tommy came out of the pool building.

38
00:02:10.731 --> 00:02:13.832
When he saw everyone staring at Kyle, he looked confused.

39
00:02:15.253 --> 00:02:16.173
"What's going on?"

40
00:02:16.553 --> 00:02:17.914
he asked, hurrying over.

41
00:02:17.934 --> 00:02:21.415
"That's a very good question," Coach Phillips said.

42
00:02:21.435 --> 00:02:25.657
"We're trying to figure out who's responsible for all of today's pranks."

43
00:02:26.797 --> 00:02:29.018
"I know the answer," Maggie declared.

44
00:02:29.979 --> 00:02:31.099
She pointed at Tommy.

45
00:02:31.119 --> 00:02:33.060
"He did it!"

46
00:02:34.044 --> 00:02:35.806
"What?" Tommy exclaimed.

47
00:02:37.367 --> 00:02:38.168
Henry winced.

48
00:02:39.208 --> 00:02:41.330
He thought Tommy was probably the culprit too.

49
00:02:42.351 --> 00:02:44.032
But they still had no way to prove it.

50
00:02:45.053 --> 00:02:47.355
Why did Maggie have to have such a big mouth?

51
00:02:48.476 --> 00:02:49.457
John looked angry.

52
00:02:49.477 --> 00:02:53.560
"How dare you accuse my brother of something like that!"

53
00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:54.941
he yelled at Maggie.

54
00:02:54.961 --> 00:02:58.344
"Tommy didn't have anything to do with this!"

55
00:02:59.905 --> 00:03:03.168
Maggie didn't back down, even though John was a lot older.

56
00:03:04.248 --> 00:03:05.609
"That's not what we think!"

57
00:03:06.049 --> 00:03:06.849
Maggie yelled back.

58
00:03:06.869 --> 00:03:08.670
"Right, Henry?"

59
00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:13.112
"I don't understand," Tommy said, looking confused.

60
00:03:14.252 --> 00:03:14.952
"What happened?

61
00:03:15.933 --> 00:03:17.253
Are the frogs in the pool again?"

62
00:03:17.273 --> 00:03:19.974
"No," Tiny told him.

63
00:03:19.994 --> 00:03:23.456
"Someone poured paint in Kyle's bag."

64
00:03:23.476 --> 00:03:29.258
"You want to make everyone think that Cole did all these pranks," Maggie went on.

65
00:03:29.278 --> 00:03:31.259
"How did you do it?"

66
00:03:31.279 --> 00:03:33.400
"That's ridiculous."

67
00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:34.581
John scowled.

68
00:03:34.601 --> 00:03:36.482
"It was Cole.

69
00:03:37.522 --> 00:03:39.703
Everyone knows he has pet frogs."

70
00:03:40.704 --> 00:03:43.185
"Right!" Lauren jumped in.

71
00:03:43.205 --> 00:03:49.249
"You probably poured that green paint in Kyle's bag too," John went on.

72
00:03:50.309 --> 00:03:51.110
He looked around.

73
00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.491
"Or maybe it was Daisy.

74
00:03:54.612 --> 00:03:56.573
Everyone knows she likes to paint!"

75
00:03:56.593 --> 00:03:59.354
"What?" Daisy cried.

76
00:03:59.374 --> 00:04:01.836
"I didn't do anything!"

77
00:04:02.976 --> 00:04:06.898
"And like I keep telling everyone, I didn't put those frogs in the pool!"

78
00:04:07.218 --> 00:04:07.958
Cole added.

79
00:04:07.978 --> 00:04:10.499
"I would never do something like that.

80
00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:13.521
Pool water isn't good for frogs!"

81
00:04:14.721 --> 00:04:16.222
Everyone started yelling at once.

82
00:04:17.482 --> 00:04:19.963
Maggie was yelling at Coach Phillips about evidence.

83
00:04:21.084 --> 00:04:23.145
John was yelling that Tommy was innocent.

84
00:04:24.305 --> 00:04:26.746
Kyle was yelling about his bag being ruined.

85
00:04:27.827 --> 00:04:30.848
Cole and Daisy were yelling that they hadn't done anything wrong.

86
00:04:32.048 --> 00:04:33.990
Everyone else was yelling out questions.

87
00:04:35.451 --> 00:04:36.752
But Henry wasn't yelling.

88
00:04:37.893 --> 00:04:38.734
He was thinking.

89
00:04:39.875 --> 00:04:42.317
Something someone had just said didn't make sense.

90
00:04:43.458 --> 00:04:44.299
That was a clue.

91
00:04:45.359 --> 00:04:45.980
A big one!

92
00:04:47.101 --> 00:04:49.423
Suddenly he realized who was behind all the trouble.

93
00:04:49.443 --> 00:04:53.106
"Hold on," he said.

94
00:04:53.126 --> 00:04:55.308
"I know who did this."

95
00:04:56.449 --> 00:04:57.330
Nobody heard him.

96
00:04:58.430 --> 00:04:59.872
Everyone else was still yelling.

97
00:05:01.324 --> 00:05:04.726
So Henry stuck his fingers in his mouth and let out a loud whistle.

98
00:05:05.827 --> 00:05:07.929
Everyone fell silent for a second.

99
00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:10.711
They all turned to look at Henry.

100
00:05:10.731 --> 00:05:14.193
"I know who did this," he said again.

101
00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:16.014
"You do?"

102
00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:17.295
Maggie asked.

103
00:05:17.315 --> 00:05:20.377
"Of course he does," Kyle said.

104
00:05:20.397 --> 00:05:22.739
"Henry is friends with Cole.

105
00:05:24.100 --> 00:05:25.641
He probably even helped Cole.

106
00:05:26.621 --> 00:05:28.703
Why else would he hang around the pool all day?"

107
00:05:28.723 --> 00:05:32.225
"Yeah." John rolled his eyes.

108
00:05:32.245 --> 00:05:35.186
"Why are we even listening to him?

109
00:05:36.207 --> 00:05:37.828
He doesn't know anything."

110
00:05:37.848 --> 00:05:40.549
"He might," Daisy said.

111
00:05:40.569 --> 00:05:44.011
"Haven't you heard about The Lemonade Detectives?

112
00:05:45.552 --> 00:05:49.434
Henry and his friends helped my neighbor find his lost keys last week."

113
00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:52.115
"Really?" Tiny asked.

114
00:05:52.135 --> 00:05:54.016
"That's cool.

115
00:05:54.997 --> 00:05:57.358
Can you guys find my lost cell phone?"

116
00:05:57.378 --> 00:06:00.660
"Quiet!" Coach Phillips shouted.

117
00:06:02.144 --> 00:06:04.246
"Henry, do you really know something about all this?"

118
00:06:05.367 --> 00:06:06.148
Henry nodded.

119
00:06:06.168 --> 00:06:10.432
"Cole didn't have anything to do with the pranks," he said.

120
00:06:10.452 --> 00:06:13.956
"Neither did Daisy or Kyle or Tommy."

121
00:06:13.976 --> 00:06:16.078
"Then who did it?"

122
00:06:16.438 --> 00:06:17.259
Maggie asked.

123
00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.362
Henry looked over at Tommy's brother.

124
00:06:20.382 --> 00:06:22.344
"It was John."
